0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Found reviewing #802 (present before it; the rebuild in #802 only carries it forward). In UNIFIED_INGREDIENT_MAPPING.tsv, 'Na2HPO4·7H2O' and 'K2HPO4 x 3H2O' carry the anhydrous CHEBI ids. That is a hydrate→anhydrous identity collapse, which MAPPING_SEMANTICS forbids. Needs tracing to whether the claw builder or the MIM records supply those ids.\n\n---\n**Traced:** the claw builder ranked a recipe's own `term.id` above MIM's ruling on the label. Fix in progress: CultureBotAI/culturebotai-claw#571 resolves through MIM's label index first, which fixes `K2HPO4 x 3H2O`'s `mim_id` and about 58 other hydrate labels. Still open after it: (a) the `chebi_id` column keeps the recipe's anhydrous CHEBI term when MIM's identity is a non-CHEBI mint (a deliberate `_published_ids` rule; kg-microbe#723 / #138); (b) `Na2HPO4·7H2O` has no label-index row (#811).","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/808/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/808/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}